format session-log-v1
stamp 20260820.021400
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan abandon -- a conferral whose holder fell served nobody, and the run says so
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; condense REMEMBER when a set closes; send each finished increment
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows read whole -- %88, %89, %90, %92, %93, %94 all closed on metal or by a host hand, and %91 superseded by %93 with the 514-page room sweep. No agent-closable red stands open, so the corrective queue is empty and the constructive one may open.
think The last lap's recommend named the crux already: a dependent that falls holding conferred reach can answer for nothing. Reading confer, revoke, and reclaim together, all three weigh what a dependent may touch -- at the front of its life, at the back of a standing one, and after it is gone. None of them asks what became of the work the conferral was granted for.
think The hole is in the accounting rather than on the wire. reclaim takes a conferral back the moment its holder is reaped, whether the holder came home or fell, and the run has already counted the conferred phase as absorbed -- which is the record's word for taken up, which is its word for carried. A plan whose author declared a fall reads back as a plan fully carried out.
think That names the fourth member of a family the arc built three of: dark reach before the door weighed it, stale reach after the work came home, inherited reach at a successor's first breath, and abandoned reach -- what a run conferred that nobody served. The other three count a hazard; this one alone counts a loss.
think Where the answer lives decides whether the rung is real. A count kept in the supervisor is the supervisor's claim about itself, and the process holding it exits. So the count is written into the departed domain's own notes after the reclamation has swept them clean -- surviving the very act that erases every other trace of the conferral -- and read back before the report believes it.
think The dependent needed something it had never been given. A plan names the outcome it expects of every phase, and only the supervisor ever read that word; the window this rung studies opens inside a dependent's own life, after it grafts a conferral and before it carries the work. So the declaration rides the same wire as the pruning promise, written before the spawn and read at the graft.
think The first cut of the lap went RED honestly, and the guard is what said so. The falling dependent was written second, the door refused it beside a standing sibling that contends over the shared board region, and the run passed its conferring phase ahead as a dependent of its own -- so the holder fell holding nothing and abandoned reach read 0 against 0. The plan was reordered rather than the guard softened.
think Two RED paths refused to build rather than to run, exactly as last lap taught -- dropping a refusal outright makes its parameter unused. Falsifying the condition in place while keeping the parameter read is what makes the proof a proof.
think TAME's ratchet printed three functions past 70 lines once the rung grew, all of them in code this round touched. Each split at a natural seam -- the record seating, the dependent's own line, the graft of promised reach, and the return a pruning asks back -- and every one of the four reads better alone than it did inline.
obs The rung buys no speed and no room, as confer, revoke, and reclaim did not. It buys the last quarter of the honesty claim: the arc now answers what a dependent may touch before the door weighs it, while it stands, after its work comes home, after it is gone -- and now what its going cost.
obs Every number but one stands still across the two runs, and that is what makes the finding a finding rather than a difference between two different plans. Four phases, three dependents, one carried home, one conferred, one reclaimed, one absorbed -- identical. Only the answer for the lost work moves, and the 0 is the false one.
obs The choir named tools/caravan_harvest_witness.rish RED once and then ran GREEN four times over, including a full 54-rung sing and a deliberate cold-tree solo. Not reproduced, so nothing is claimed about it and no row is booked; recorded here plainly because a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, and this one has fired once.
obs The council rota read this lap was item 9, the Pond foundation. Its line about customs -- that at receipt each mark earns place, hold, or refuse -- is the same shape as this rung read from the other end: a run that accepts work must be able to say what it did with it.
loom witness=caravan_abandon_witness rungs=54 phases=4 dependents=3 carried_home=1 conferred=1 reclaimed=1 absorbed=1 abandoned_silent=0 abandoned_answered=1 red_paths_proven=5
file caravan/abandon.rye the rung -- abandoned reach, the declaration a dependent now reads, four refusals, and the count written to the wire after the sweep
file tools/caravan_abandon_witness.rish the witness on metal, reading the selftest natively and naming all five proven RED paths
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir registration, so the bijection stands at 54 and no rung sings unheard
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, beside reclaim, in the same commit as the code it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge seated, the rung below folded to prior
recommend keep-going the arc has answered for reach at every moment of a dependent's life; the next question is the supervisor's own -- a run that abandons work knows what was lost yet never says whether the plan should have been run at all, so a record that refuses to report itself complete while an arc it absorbed bought nothing is the mirror of this rung.
